"el": "Το ποιόν ενεργείας στην πράξη",
"title": "Aspect in practice: choosing the right stem",
"span": "B1–B2",
"blurb": "One decision runs through every Greek verb: the ongoing stem (γράφ-) or the one-off stem (γράψ-). This chapter drills the choice everywhere it appears: after να and θα, past narration (imperfect or aorist), commands and prohibitions, with time words (πάντα, ξαφνικά, για δύο ώρες), and in the minimal pairs where the meaning changes (θα τρώω / θα φάω, μην τρως / μη φας).",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Chapter 16 introduced aspect, and chapters 17–23 apply it tense by tense. In real speech you meet it all at once. Each section below is a set of **minimal pairs**: two sentences that differ only in the stem, with the difference in meaning spelled out, followed by drills that mix the cases. Ask yourself one question each time: **is the action seen as a whole, done once (one-off stem), or as ongoing, repeated or habitual (ongoing stem)**?"
},
